# ============================================================================
# CyberPulseAcademy - .gitignore
#
# Read the final section before adding a rule here. Several files in this
# repository ARE generated output and ARE committed on purpose, because GitHub
# Pages serves them directly and because the build workflow commits them back.
# Ignoring one of them silently breaks the published site.
# ============================================================================


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system files
#
# Cruft that the OS creates, which no contributor intended to commit. Thumbs.db
# and desktop.ini come from Windows Explorer, .DS_Store from macOS Finder. The
# AppleDouble pattern covers the "._filename" resource-fork companions that
# macOS writes onto non-HFS volumes such as USB sticks and network shares: they
# look like real files, they are binary junk, and they are a common accidental
# commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.VolumeIcon.icns


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and IDEs
#
# Per-editor state and scratch files. None of this is project configuration,
# and the project does not ship a workspace file for any editor: contributors
# use different tools and none of them should be imposed on the others.
#
# Note that this ignores the whole .vscode/ and .idea/ folders. If the project
# ever needs to share an editor setting with everyone, commit the single
# specific file with a negation rule (for example "!.vscode/settings.json")
# rather than un-ignoring the folder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python artifacts
#
# Byte-compiled output, virtual environments and tool caches. The build scripts
# are standard library only, so a virtual environment is never required to run
# them; contributors who do create one should keep it out of the repository.
#
# scripts/__pycache__/ is generated the first time any script imports another
# script (validate.py imports build_catalog.py), so it appears locally almost
# immediately and must never be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The optional Pillow install marker
#
# Pillow is the single optional dependency in this project, used only by
# generate_og.py --png and --icons, and deliberately never installed by CI.
# A contributor who installs it locally may leave a marker or a locally
# generated wheel behind; neither belongs in the repository. The dependency
# itself is declared in scripts/requirements.txt, which IS committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PIL/
Pillow/
pillow-*.tar.gz
pillow-*.whl
Pillow-*.whl


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node artifacts, just in case
#
# This project has no package.json, no npm scripts and no Node dependency, and
# the site is deliberately buildless. These rules exist only so that a future
# tool added by a contributor cannot accidentally commit a dependency tree.
# If a package.json is ever added on purpose, this section should be revisited
# and the lockfile decision made explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build scratch output
#
# scripts/generate_pages.py writes an intermediate cache of parsed topic data
# to data/.cache/topics.json so repeated runs are fast. It is pure scratch:
# deleting it costs nothing but a slower next run, and it must never be
# committed because it is a derived duplicate of data/<type>/*.json.
#
# The generated artifacts that matter are listed in the final section below,
# and they are NOT in this directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/.cache/
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment and secret files
#
# Nothing secret may ever be committed to this repository. Everything served by
# GitHub Pages is public by definition, so a credential placed in a shipped
# file is a credential disclosed. The one credential the site uses is a PayPal
# *hosted button id*, which is designed to be publishable; a PayPal client
# secret, an API key, a webhook signing secret or a database connection string
# is not, and must never appear in this repository in any file.
#
# These rules are the backstop, not the policy. The policy is in README.md and
# CONTRIBUTING.md: no secrets in client-side code, ever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.local
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Worker local state
#
# If a statistics endpoint is built with a Cloudflare Worker, local development
# produces a .wrangler/ state directory and, for `wrangler dev`, a .dev.vars
# file holding local secrets. Neither belongs in the repository. The Worker
# source itself would be committed; its local state and its secrets would not.
#
# Note that cloudflare-worker/ currently exists in this repository but is
# empty: no Worker is implemented yet. These rules are here so that the state
# cannot be committed by accident when one is added.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.wrangler/
wrangler.toml.bak


# ============================================================================
# DO NOT IGNORE THESE: generated artifacts that are committed on purpose
#
# The files below are build output, but they are tracked deliberately. GitHub
# Pages serves them as-is, and the CI workflow regenerates them and expects the
# committed copies to match: if the generator produces different content and it
# has not been committed, the workflow fails with "Generated files are stale".
#
# Listing them here as negations is self-documenting. Do not remove these lines,
# and do not add a broad rule above (such as "*.json" or "*.xml") that would
# swallow them.
#
#   data/catalog.json     The manifest carrying all 246 topic objects. The
#                         entire site reads it at runtime; without it the site
#                         loads no topics at all.
#   sitemap.xml           Generated by build_catalog.py. Served to crawlers and
#                         referenced from robots.txt.
#   robots.txt            Generated by build_catalog.py. Carries the crawler
#                         directives and the sitemap pointer.
#   assets/img/og/*       The per-topic Open Graph social cards. Generated by
#                         generate_og.py, and served to social platforms and
#                         search engines as the link preview image.
#
# The generated topics/*.html pages are also committed, by the same reasoning:
# they are what GitHub Pages actually serves. They are not ignored above, and
# they must not be.
# ============================================================================
!data/catalog.json
!sitemap.xml
!robots.txt
!assets/img/og/*.svg
!assets/img/og/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual Studio local state.
#
# .vs/ holds Visual Studio's own file index and per-user settings. It is not
# part of this project, it grows to several megabytes, and it must never be
# committed. GitHub Desktop will show it as untracked until this rule is
# present, and a stray commit of it would add thousands of binary files to the
# repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
*.vsidx

# JetBrains local state.
.idea/
